{
 "version": 1,
 "point": "date.table",
 "note": "Reviewer-written labels for the date.table replay (T268, M4 point 3). Each item is one model: its tables (name, columns as Name:Type, a CALENDAR formula when it is a calculated table), relationships (many>one), measures (Table|Name|DAX), an optional calculation group, and the derived facts a live model would measure ('day' one row per day with none missing, 'repeats' a date on more than one row, 'gaps' no repeats but a day missing; absent means not measured, as a model opened from files). The label is what a model author should decide: a table name, 'generate' or 'none', and whether to mark it; alsoOk lists another acceptable answer. Shapes come from the UAT fixtures Northstar and ContosoMini, an AdventureWorks-style sample and synthetic Contoso-style cases. No real model, tenant or person names. Labels were written before any rule or Jev answer was seen.",
